        "original_id": "37339adb-3726-5356-8c84-cfa3337efb87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: The Kabalas\n- Places: Quad Cities, American Mid-West, Europe, the Americas, Czech\n- Concepts: Klezmer, Jewish folksongs, Israeli popular songs, Polka, popular music, dance music\n\nFacts:\n- The Kabalas were a four-piece band from the Quad Cities area of the American Mid-West.\n- The Kabalas based their music firmly in a traditional Eastern European Klezmer style.\n- The Kabalas mixed Jewish folksongs, Israeli popular songs, Polka, and popular music into their Klezmer-based style.\n- Polka is originally a Czech dance and a genre of dance music.\n- Polka is familiar throughout Europe and the Americas.",
